    dmo:evidenceQuote "The lenses within our eyes are clear structures that help provide sharp vision—but they tend to become cloudy as we age. People with diabetes are more likely to develop cloudy lenses, called cataracts." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Your chances of developing glaucoma or cataracts are about twice that of someone without diabetes." ;
